    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6fbf56a4-feff-500f-9247-5e82e76f3649",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+210^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter exact coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\sin(x+210^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+210^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 210^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 210^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe plus sign outside the second blank is supplied. The entries are $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $-\\frac{1}{2}$, respectively.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
